cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "GhostLM: a from-scratch cybersecurity language model on a transparent scale ladder"
message: "If you reference GhostLM in research or downstream tooling, please cite this repository."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Munene
    given-names: Joe
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"  # placeholder; will be filled when assigned
repository-code: "https://github.com/joemunene-by/GhostLM"
url: "https://huggingface.co/Ghostgim/GhostLM-v0.9-experimental"
abstract: >-
  GhostLM is a decoder-only transformer language model built entirely
  from scratch in PyTorch and trained on a curated cybersecurity
  corpus (NVD CVEs, MITRE ATT&CK, CWE, CAPEC, OWASP, IETF RFCs,
  CTFtime writeups, PRIMUS, NIST SP 800, plus general-language and
  math-reasoning shards in the v1.0 corpus). The project is
  organized as a transparent multi-rung scale ladder
  (ghost-tiny 14.7M, ghost-small 45-81M, ghost-base ~360M target,
  ghost-1B / ghost-3B / ghost-7B in subsequent rungs). All training
  code, evaluation harnesses, corpus collectors, and benchmark
  results are public. The project explicitly avoids fine-tuning on
  top of pretrained weights so the codebase doubles as a readable
  reference implementation.
keywords:
  - language model
  - cybersecurity
  - from-scratch
  - transformer
  - pytorch
  - small model
  - cti
  - mitre attack
  - cve
  - ctibench
license: MIT
version: "0.9.3"
date-released: "2026-05-07"
